:: D04_Evening_Cook [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Stirring pasta sauce at the small kitchen stove" "banner" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/d04-cooking.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The bananas are perfect, ripe, sweet, exactly what I wanted. I eat two standing at the counter, and the craving quiets like a satisfied animal. Marcus would have grabbed a gas station hot dog. This body wants fruit and warmth and things that taste clean.</p>

<p>I decide to actually cook, not microwave ramen, not eat cereal from the box. The kitchen has pasta and a can of tomato sauce, both sealed, both older than this week. I find a pot, fill it with water, put it on the burner.</p>

<p>While the water heats I chop a banana into coins and eat them one by one. The kitchen window lets in afternoon light going golden. The apartment is quiet except for the burner clicking and traffic outside and the faint sound of music from the upstairs neighbor.</p>

<p>The water boils. I dump in the pasta, stir it with a fork since I don't own a wooden spoon, and set a timer on my phone. Eight minutes.</p>

<p>While it cooks I heat the sauce in a smaller pot and stir it. It pops and spatters and I jump back, which makes me laugh at myself. I'm a grown adult scared of tomato sauce.</p>

<p>When it's done I drain the pasta in the sink using the pot lid as a strainer, since there's no colander in this apartment and never has been. I dump the sauce on top and stir.</p>

</div>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Eating spaghetti alone at the small kitchen table, golden evening light" "float" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/d04-eating-table.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I sit at the kitchen table, small, meant for one person, pushed against the wall under the window. Marcus ate on the couch, always, every meal, phone in one hand, fork in the other, something streaming on the laptop. But tonight I sit at the table.</p>

<p>The pasta is basic, overcooked by a minute, sauce from a can, no seasoning because the spice rack is nonexistent. But it's warm and I made it and I'm eating it sitting at a table like a human being who lives here, who belongs here, who is choosing to be present in this moment instead of hiding from it.</p>

<p>Something about the act feels like a small reclamation. Not feminine, not masculine. Just alive.</p>

<p>I eat slowly, watch the light change through the window. When I'm done I wash the dishes, both pots, the fork, the plate, dry them, put them away.</p>

<p>The kitchen is clean. It might be the first time the kitchen has been clean since Marcus moved in.</p>

</div>

<<set $d04CookedMeal to true>>
<<set $timeslot to "Evening">>
<<run window.statChange("fem", 1)>>
<<run window.rbAddMilestone("Cooked a real meal and sat down to eat it.")>>

