:: D04_FallAsleep [nobr]
<div class="prose-block">

<p>I fall asleep faster tonight. The body is learning to sleep, learning to eat, to walk, to sit, to be. Four days in, and the crisis is mellowing into something that might, if I squint, look like the beginning of a life.</p>

<p>The dream comes back. The same hallway of mirrors from two nights ago, long and narrow, lit from above by fluorescent tubes that flicker and buzz. Every reflection is still me, wearing something different each time. This time the one in the red dress is closer than she was before, close enough that I can see she's smiling before I even reach for her.</p>

<p>I reach anyway. She reaches back.</p>

<p>I wake up and don't remember the dream for three hours. But my face is wet, and I think I was smiling in my sleep this time, not crying.</p>

</div>

